  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Upper low over the Great Lakes will move \nsoutheast tonight then pull off to the northeast Monday. Showers\nand thunderstorms will move through the northern tier \nperiodically through early Tuesday.\n\nA 70 kt jet max at 500 mb rounding the base of the upper trough\nover the Great Lakes will provide deep synoptic lift for an area\nof rain with embedded thunderstorms pivoting across NW PA\ntonight. Storms have been severe warned in Ohio as they have\ncome off Lake Erie, but they are expected to weaken\nsignificantly as they move southeastward towards central PA.\nThere is some degree of west-east training with these storms, so\nnorthwestern Warren Co may end up seeing as much as 0.75-1.00 \nof rain, mostly falling before 2 AM. Less rainfall is expected \nto the south and east, with little to none south of I-80 and \neast of the Laurels. \n\nWe expect less coverage of SHRA/TSRA Monday without good PVA \nmoving across. However, the cold pool aloft and heating should \nmake isolated to scattered convection along at least the \nnorthern tier. It is unlikely that any precip will get south of\nI-80, but there will be plenty of clouds. Some showers will \nlinger into the night and possibly early Tuesday before drier \nair works in as the upper trough departs.",
